    {
      "id": "h9732y4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO PUBLIC FINANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Public Finance covers public revenue, public expenditure, government budgets, deficits, public debt, and the Finance Commission.",
        "Public Revenue is broadly categorized into Tax Revenue (Direct and Indirect Taxes) and Non-Tax Revenue.",
        "Government budgets track expenditure and revenue, with key deficit metrics measuring fiscal health.",
        "Major deficits analyzed in competitive exams include Revenue Deficit, Fiscal Deficit, and Primary Deficit.",
        "Deficit financing and public debt are essential instruments used by governments to bridge spending gaps.",
        "The Finance Commission manages fiscal federalism and resource distribution between the Centre and States."
      ],
      "id": "r5hdq40"
    },
